    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="0793" n="783" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg783"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50/9–244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-02T17:00:00+02:00">September 2,
                            1944—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 2—2:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7184. For Berle, Hooker and Radius.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>A slight alteration is proposed in the procedure outlined in Embassy’s
                        7096, August 31. In showing Draft B of communication (see Embassy’s 7097,
                        August 31) to Soviet Government, Foreign Office thinks delay might result if
                        concurrence of Soviet Government is sought to the words in paragraph 4
                        referring to its attitude. It is proposed instead to tell the Soviet
                        Government that if it is not ready to join in the communication, Draft B
                        will be circulated to the Allies. If the Soviet Government should volunteer
                        any objections, they would, of course, be taken into account in the
                        procedure followed.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Foreign Office urgently wishes to know if the Department agrees with its
                        view that invitations to the EITO Conference should be addressed to the
                        following: The Governments of the Netherlands, Luxembourg, Czechoslovakia,
                        Poland, Yugoslavia, Greece and Norway and the French Committee of National
                        Liberation. It is further proposed to ask the Danish Legation here if it
                        wishes to be represented by an observer.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
